# Paths that may hold a Key Vault secret data-plane command (check-manual-keyvault.py).
# Policy `secrets-write-only-entry` — Doc/Architecture/SecretsWriteOnlyEntry.
#
# Each line: <glob>  — <why this path may hold one>. The list only SHRINKS: an entry that no longer
# matches a file holding a vault command is stale and reds the gate. A doc or runbook NEVER goes
# here — a documented break-glass procedure carries the `kv-break-glass` marker instead.

deploy/aks/operator/bin/*  — the GOVERNED implementation: the operator verbs an InstanceAction runs (hosting-kv-set/-status/-state as the writer identity; the provisioning verbs still on hosting-operator are the migration's step 3)
deploy/aks/operator/test/*  — the behaviour suite that proves those verbs write through --file, never print a value and never read one back
deploy/aks/operator/test/stubs/*/az  — stand-in az binaries for that suite; they answer the commands, they do not run them
.github/scripts/check-manual-keyvault.py  — this gate, which has to spell the commands it refuses
